  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-15",
    "scope": "Three useful Commons2023 west-front, north-side rooftop and nave-transept rooftop photographs plus standard viewer PMTiles/DEM. Photographs viewed only, not downloaded or redistributed. No bespoke drawings/surveys researched.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucca_Cattedrale_di_San_Martino_Esterno_Facciata_%26_Campanile_4.jpg",
        "author": "Zairon",
        "date": "2023-04-21",
        "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected west-front photograph: two large round portico arches and a smaller southern arch against the campanile; deep shaded vaults and recessed door portals. Three marble arcade tiers, lowest two full-width and upper narrower, with thin columns, varied round arches, gray-green horizontal inlay strips and geometric diamonds. Southwest tower has tan brick below, pale marble upper tiers, graduated1/2/3/4 arched openings and merlons. Fine sculptures and carved columns are not reproduced exactly."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucca_Chiesa_dei_Santi_Giovanni_e_Reparata_Campanile_Vista_su_la_Cattedrale_di_San_Martino_4.jpg",
        "author": "Zairon",
        "date": "2023-04-21",
        "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected north-side elevated photograph: long pale nave above lower aisle, high circular clerestory windows, blind round arcades and gray horizontal striping. Repeated stone ribs rise above reddish tiled lean-to aisle roof. Tall north transept has circular high windows and a lower round arched portal. Stone diamonds below eaves, simple red tile gables, side buttress rhythm. Exact carving and hidden joins remain approximate."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucca_Cattedrale_di_San_Martino_Campanile_Vista_su_la_Cattedrale_2.jpg",
        "author": "Zairon",
        "date": "2023-04-21",
        "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected elevated view from campanile: red/brown tile long nave gable joins cross transept gable at common ridge; low lean-to aisles with repeated stone ribs. Transept sides have circular windows, blind arcades and sparse stone diamonds near eaves. Flat marble walls below red tiled roofs; no dominant dome. Rear apse roof is estimated from mapped round outline and main roof character."
      }
    ]
  }
